{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 79,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.79.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.79.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A Psalm of Asaph. O God, the heathen have come into thy inheritance; thy holy temple have they defiled; they have laid Jerusalem on heaps.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.79.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.79.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The dead bodies of thy servants have they given ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " food to the fowls of the heaven, the flesh of thy saints, to the beasts of the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.79.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.79.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their blood have they shed like water around Jerusalem; and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none to bury ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.79.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.79.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We have become a reproach to our neighbors, a scorn and derision to them that are around us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.79.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.79.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How long, LORD? wilt thou be angry for ever? shall thy jealousy burn like fire?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.79.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.79.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Pour out thy wrath upon the heathen that have not known thee, and upon the kingdoms that have not called upon thy name.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.79.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.79.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For they have devoured Jacob, and laid waste his dwelling-place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.79.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.79.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O remember not against us former iniquities: let thy tender mercies speedily succor us: for we are brought very low.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.79.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.79.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Help us, O God of our salvation, for the glory of thy name: and deliver us, and purge away our sins, for thy name's sake.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.79.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.79.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why should the heathen say, Where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their God? let him be known among the heathen in our sight ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "by",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " avenging the blood of thy servants ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.79.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.79.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let the sighing of the prisoner come before thee; according to the greatness of thy power preserve thou those that are appointed to die;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.79.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.79.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And render to our neighbors seven-fold into their bosom their reproach, with which they have reproached thee, O LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.79.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.79.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So we thy people and sheep of thy pasture will give thee thanks for ever: we will show forth thy praise to all generations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
